Morbstack's own source (mac/, guest/morbinit/, proto/, scripts/) has no
third-party dependencies: `mac/Package.swift` links only Foundation and
system frameworks (no Swift packages are resolved), and
`guest/morbinit/Cargo.toml` declares an empty `[dependencies]` table (Rust
std only). Nothing below is compiled into the `morbstackd`, `morb`, or
`morbinit` binaries themselves; it is unmodified upstream software that
Morbstack's guest VM runs alongside its own code, or that Morbstack's
tooling fetches as a build/runtime input.

## What is actually in this git repository

None of the binaries listed below are committed to this repository.
`.gitignore` excludes everything under `dist/` except the `PROVENANCE.txt`
files and `dist/CROSS_COMPILE.md` — the repository tracks the *record* of
what was fetched, from where, and with which cryptographic hash, not the
bytes themselves. `scripts/fetch-guest-assets.sh` re-downloads and
re-verifies every item below against the pins recorded in that script and
in the corresponding `dist/*/PROVENANCE.txt` file. A `git clone` of
Morbstack alone contains none of this NOTICE's third-party redistributed
material; a *built* `Morbstack.app` or guest disk image does, because
`mise run guest-image` assembles the boot image and `morb k8s enable` streams
the Kubernetes payload into a running guest.

