## On the GPL-2.0 Linux kernel specifically

The guest kernel is GPL-2.0-only, unmodified, and fetched as a prebuilt
binary from kata-containers' own public release — it is not modified,
recompiled, or statically linked with any Apache-2.0-licensed Morbstack
code. It runs as a separate operating system inside a
`Virtualization.framework` VM, communicating with the macOS host only over
vsock; nothing in `mac/` or `guest/morbinit/` is compiled against kernel
headers or linked into the kernel image. Anyone who redistributes a built
Morbstack guest image is also redistributing this kernel binary and must
be able to satisfy GPL-2.0's corresponding-source obligation for it — in
practice this is already met because kata-containers publishes the kernel
as an unmodified, sourced, versioned public release; Morbstack does not
patch it and has no source changes of its own to offer.

